<title>GERMANY: BOE's George &quot;very pleased&quot; with UK rate hike.</title>
<headline>BOE's George &quot;very pleased&quot; with UK rate hike.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England governor Eddie George said on Tuesday he was very pleased with the decision by Britain to raise its minimum lending rate by a quarter of a point to 6.00 percent last Wednesday.</p>
<p>Asked for a reaction to the move as he left a meeting of the council of the European Monetary Institute in Frankfurt, George replied: &quot;Very pleased&quot;.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
